Day 3 — AWS VPC + Networking + Security

STAR approach Interview Questions

1️⃣ You need to design a secure multi-tier VPC (web/app/db). How will you architect networking, routing, and security?

2️⃣ An EC2 instance in a private subnet cannot access the internet. What steps will you take to fix this?

3️⃣ Your VPC is flat and all resources can communicate freely. How will you enforce segmentation and least-privilege networking?

4️⃣ You have 50+ VPCs across multiple environments. How will you set up scalable and secure inter-VPC connectivity?

5️⃣ For hybrid connectivity, when will you choose Site-to-Site VPN vs Direct Connect?

6️⃣ A partner needs access to one internal service without accessing your VPC. How will you design this?

7️⃣ Your application must restrict traffic based on geographic regions. Which AWS services will you use?

8️⃣ An internal service behind a private load balancer must be accessible globally. How will you redesign the architecture?

9️⃣ When will you choose an ALB vs NLB vs Gateway Load Balancer in production scenarios?

🔟 Your application requires SSL termination + routing rules + autoscaling support. Which load balancer fits best?

1️⃣1️⃣ Load balancer health checks are failing unexpectedly. How will you troubleshoot?

1️⃣2️⃣ Employees must access internal apps securely from remote locations. How will you design this?

1️⃣3️⃣ AWS WAF is blocking legitimate traffic. What corrective actions will you take?

1️⃣4️⃣ Your NAT Gateway costs are rising. How can VPC Endpoints reduce cost and improve security?

1️⃣5️⃣ You need secure microservice-to-microservice communication across VPCs. What architecture will you choose?
